# `F` at layer grain, for the parts that cross a document. One row per foreign part edge: which
# composed layer, and which layer of which other filing it is composed from.
#
# The widest `demoted`, promoted back to a reference
#   A `callActivity` names a process, so layer-grain edges collapse to document pairs, and the
#   layer survives only inside `@name` as `labour <- merge-us-member/labour`: readable by a person,
#   unresolvable by a tool. `tRelationship` carries `source` and `target` as QNames,
#   `minOccurs 1 maxOccurs unbounded`, plus a required `type` string.
#
# Why a relationship and not an `association`
#   The `type` attribute is the whole reason. An association has no name and no type, so its only
#   discriminators are its endpoints, and a second use makes two facts indistinguishable. That is
#   exercised rather than feared: `merge-group-composition` and `merge-holding-composition` would
#   each carry coupling lines and part lines side by side, in the two documents where *a coupling
#   is never evidence for a fusion* matters most. A relationship says which relation it is, in a
#   required field.
#
# The `extensionElements` refusal does not reach this
#   That refusal is *ForeignId crosses by naming a position in the other document and never by
#   importing any of it, and an extension element is importing all of it*. A relationship carries
#   two QNames and a type string: it names positions and imports nothing. The refusal was about a
#   content model, not about a chapter of the standard.
#
# Foreign parts only
#   A local part is a `childLaneSet` and already keyed `(filing, layer)`, so it never lost the
#   grain and owes no repair.
#
# Defined, not read
#   A program reads these columns, so this statement defines its vocabulary in its own
#   WITH clause: a view keeps the rows and loses the column's origin, which is where
#   NOT NULL lives. assets/sqlc/views.sqlc says what a definition is.
#
-- asrt:Fusion/asrt:Part crossing a document; BPMN 2.0 tRelationship source/target.
WITH
notations AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/notations.sqlc)
),
part_references AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/part_references.sqlc)
),
parts AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(composition/parts.sqlc)
),
calls AS NOT MATERIALIZED (
    :define(diagrams/calls.sqlc)
)
SELECT c.composition, c.composed_layer, c.part_filing, c.part_layer, c.part_notation
FROM (
    :compose(diagrams/calls.sqlc)
) c
WHERE NOT c.is_local
